  "headline": "Indonesian Parliament Formally Passes Asset Seizure Legislation",
  "seoTitle": "Indonesia Passes New Asset Seizure Law",
  "metaDescription": "The Indonesian House of Representatives has officially enacted the Asset Seizure Law to address corruption and various other criminal activities.",
  "aiSummaryBullets": [
    "The Indonesian House of Representatives officially enacted the Asset Seizure Law during a plenary session held on Thursday.",
    "The new legislation targets assets linked to various crimes, including corruption, drug trafficking, terrorism, and digital fraud.",
    "The law mandates the creation of specialized agencies to manage and oversee seized assets and maintains existing death penalty provisions for corruptors."
  ],
  "aiContextParagraph": "On November 19, 2026, the Indonesian House of Representatives (DPR RI) passed the Asset Seizure Law concerning proceeds from corruption and other criminal offenses. Led by Speaker Puan Maharani, the plenary session finalized the legislative process, which officials noted was completed ahead of the original target. The new legal framework establishes specific bodies tasked with managing and supervising seized assets to prevent potential misuse. According to government officials, including Minister of Administrative and Bureaucratic Reform Rini Widyantini, the law addresses previous regulatory limitations. The legislation covers a broad range of criminal activities, such as narcotics trafficking, terrorism, human trafficking, and digital fraud, while preserving the death penalty as a potential sanction for corruption. Proponents state the law includes four foundational pillars designed to ensure legal justice and facilitate the recovery of illicit assets within the country.",
